60,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, the options are here. A kitchen, a meeting space, or a quiet room. Which one stops the sound leaking through that thin wall?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, none of them fix the wall. But the invoices show we are already paying 68,000 yen. I need to see which option stops that bleeding first.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, a kitchen means we stop walking twenty-five minutes for lunch! It fixes the mess and saves time. I vote for the Open Kitchen!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, a kitchen feeds the body, but a quiet room feeds the soul. If the wall leaks, we need a place to rest, not just to eat.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shion, a quiet room ignores the daily drain. The lunch trip and the callouts show we need a space that stops the bleeding, not just a place to hide.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, a quiet room is exactly what stops the sound. If we keep talking, the wall makes it worse. I vote for the Quiet Room.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, a quiet room costs nothing to fit out, but it doesn’t stop the 68,000 yen we pay for outside hire. I need to see if that stops the bleeding.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, but a quiet room means no food! I still have to walk twenty-five minutes. I vote for the Open Kitchen to save my time.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, a kitchen is a stage, not a sanctuary. If the wall leaks, your cooking becomes a performance. I vote for the Quiet Room.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shion, a quiet room hides the drain. The callouts and lunch trip prove we need a space that stops the bleeding, not just a place to hide.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, the quiet room stops the noise complaints. The tally proves the two nearest to the door cause the mess. I stand by my vote.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, I understand the noise, but I cannot vote for a room that doesn't stop the 68,000 yen drain. I need to see the financials first.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, the kitchen stops the mess spreading to your desk! I stand by my vote for the Open Kitchen.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, the money is a symptom of our isolation. A quiet room gives us the dignity to speak without fear. I stand by my vote.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the quiet room stops the daily drain. No equipment means no callouts, and no walking means saved hours. I vote for the Quiet Room.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, the quiet room is the only option that respects the wall. I stand by my vote.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, I cannot vote yet. I need to see if the quiet room stops the 68,000 yen drain before I commit.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, the kitchen saves twenty-five minutes every day! That is real time, not just paper. I stand by my vote for the Open Kitchen.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, the quiet room is where we finally stop being strangers. I stand by my vote.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the quiet room has no equipment, so zero callouts. It stops the hidden labor drain. I stand by my vote.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
